 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Apologising: xin lỗi and thứ lỗi",
     "texto": [
      "**Xin lỗi** = sorry / excuse me. It's used to get someone's attention or to apologise for something small: **Xin lỗi, tôi đến trễ.** = Sorry for arriving late.",
      "**thứ lỗi** / **tha lỗi** = to really forgive, when you've done something wrong: **Xin bà thứ lỗi.** = Please forgive me, madam.",
      "A child to his father: **Con xin lỗi ba, ba tha lỗi cho con.** = Sorry, Dad, forgive me.",
      "To reply: **Không sao.** = It's nothing / no problem.",
      "• The hostess who hasn't come out to greet because she's been cooking will say: **Xin ông bà thứ lỗi, tôi bận làm cơm nên bây giờ mới ra chào ông bà được.**"
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Double words typical of home",
     "texto": [
      "Vietnamese joins two words to sound more natural or to create another idea:",
      "**cơm nước** = food (everything) · **nhà cửa** = the house, the home · **bàn ghế** = furniture (table + chair) · **mua bán** = shopping (buying + selling) · **làm ăn** = to make a living (working + eating).",
      "**Cơm nước xong rồi, xin mời ông bà vào xơi cơm.** = Food's ready, please come in and eat. (**xơi** = to eat, very respectful.)"
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
